From 50cb2ccbef7d84852f2600bb4d3e69f6bd736561 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ravindu644 <droidcasts@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Feb 2026 22:27:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Droidspaces/LXC: fix: restore cgroup file prefix handling for
 Droidspaces/LXC compatibility

Android mounts cgroup v1 with noprefix, so the cpuset files are called cpus and mems
while runc asks for cpuset.cpus and cpuset.mems. Expose the controller-prefixed name as
a link alongside the unprefixed original.

Adapted on 2026-10-13 for the kernel this repository ships, from
sm8150-samsung/android_kernel_samsung_sm8150-common at branch lineage-18.1 (Linux
4.14.190). The upstream hunk targets a newer kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c, so it was
re-anchored by hand against that tree. The change itself is upstream's, unmodified.

Upstream commit:  50cb2ccbef7d84852f2600bb4d3e69f6bd736561
Upstream file:    Documentation/resources/kernel-patches/non-GKI/02.fix_restore
                  cgroup file prefix handling .patch
Upstream project: https://github.com/ravindu644/Droidspaces-OSS

Signed-off-by: ravindu644 <droidcasts@protonmail.com>
Signed-off-by: builder <builder@localhost>
---
 kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
index 8c3850ab1..7adc5ff0a 100755
--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
@@ -3592,6 +3592,21 @@ static int cgroup_add_file(struct cgroup_subsys_state *css, struct cgroup *cgrp,
 		spin_unlock_irq(&cgroup_file_kn_lock);
 	}
 
+	/* Droidspaces: restore the controller-prefixed cgroup file name
+	 *
+	 * Android mounts cgroup v1 with noprefix, so the cpuset files are called
+	 * "cpus"/"mems" rather than "cpuset.cpus"/"cpuset.mems". runc asks the kernel
+	 * for the prefixed names and fails with ENOENT, which makes every
+	 * `docker run` inside a container impossible:
+	 *   open /sys/fs/cgroup/cpuset/docker/cpuset.cpus: No such file or directory
+	 * Provide them as links alongside the unprefixed originals.
+	 */
+	if (cft->ss && (cgrp->root->flags & CGRP_ROOT_NOPREFIX) &&
+	    !(cft->flags & CFTYPE_NO_PREFIX)) {
+		snprintf(name, CGROUP_FILE_NAME_MAX, "%s.%s", cft->ss->name, cft->name);
+		kernfs_create_link(cgrp->kn, name, kn);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
